    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10530" root="خزل" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْزَلُ</span></b>  <i>Having a fracture in his back;</i> as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَخْزُولٌ</span></b> : (O, K:) or <i>having a fracture in the
middle of his back;</i> as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الظَّهْرِ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَخْزُولُ</span></b> . (Lth,
TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And A camel <i>whose hump has entirely
gone away:</i> (K:) so says Lth; but Az thinks
that this may be a mistranscription for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجْزَلُ</span>; or
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ج</span> may be interchangeable in this case.
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also <i>Lame.</i> (AA, TA.)

